WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你制作了终极版《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室女士》。

8
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:25.390
Hey, everybody.
嘿，大家好。

9
00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:26.890
Welcome to Office Ladies.
欢迎收听《办公室女士》。

10
00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:28.050
Bonjour.
Bonjour（你好）。

11
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:29.550
Bonjour.
Bonjour（你好）。

12
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:30.710
I don't know.
我也不知道。

13
00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.290
I don't know.
我也不知道。

14
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:39.930
I am wearing, like, this T-shirt is kind of, like, it's, like, really soft and shimmery, but it's, like, also feels like pajamas.
我身上穿的这件T恤，怎么说呢，它摸起来真的很柔软、很有光泽，但穿起来又感觉像睡衣一样。

15
00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.530
And I think it's just got me in a, I don't know, in a mood to say bonjour.
我觉得这让我进入了一种……我不知道，一种想说Bonjour的心情。

16
00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:47.930
Angela, when I first saw you, I thought you were just wearing a black T-shirt.
安吉拉，我刚看到你的时候，以为你只是穿了一件黑色T恤。

17
00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:52.930
And I was really disappointed because I showed up in my Pam teapot shirt for our recording.
我当时真的很失望，因为我为了录音特意穿了我的“帕姆茶壶”T恤。

18
00:00:53.470 --> 00:01:00.210
Why I like to always wear an Office Ladies or Office-themed or use an Office mug when we record, I don't know.
为什么我录音时总喜欢穿《办公室女士》或《办公室》主题的衣服，或者用《办公室》的马克杯，我也不知道。

19
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:00.990
It's a thing.
这是一种习惯。

20
00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.450
It's, like, you want to get in the mindset.
就像是，你想进入那种状态。

21
00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:03.630
Here's the thing, guys.
是这样的，伙计们。

22
00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.610
Every single week, Jenna shows up.
每周，珍娜都会准时出现。

23
00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.550
We hop on the Zoomy Zoom because that's our life right now.
我们连上Zoom，因为这就是我们现在的生活方式。

24
00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:12.230
And she has on an Office-themed something.
她身上总会穿点《办公室》主题的东西。

25
00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:13.170
Shirt, hoodie.
衬衫，或者连帽衫。

26
00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.790
And you did this also when we used to go in the studio.
以前我们去录音棚的时候你也这样。

27
00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:16.950
You would always have your hoodie.
你总是穿着你的连帽衫。

28
00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:21.970
And today, I was like, I better dress to match my lady friend.
今天我就想，我最好穿得跟我这位好姐妹搭一点。

29
00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:27.870
Well, I thought you were wearing a black T-shirt, and then you started dancing to our theme song when it played.
好吧，我以为你穿的是件黑T恤，结果主题曲响起时你开始跟着跳舞。

30
00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.230
And I saw that it says Office Ladies.
我才看到上面写着“办公室女士”。

31
00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:31.970
I wore our Office Ladies shirt.
我穿了我们的《办公室女士》T恤。

32
00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:32.790
Made me so happy.
这让我太开心了。

33
00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:35.050
And then it made you speak French, so.
然后它让你说起了法语，所以。

34
00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:37.510
Wait, what are we here to talk about, Jenna?
等等，我们今天要聊什么来着，珍娜？

35
00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:46.610
We are here to talk about Initiation, Season 3, Episode 5, written by BJ Novak and directed by Randall Einhorn.
我们今天要聊的是《入职仪式》，第三季第五集，由BJ·诺瓦克编剧，兰德尔·艾因霍恩执导。

36
00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:49.070
There are a lot of good quotes in this one.
这一集里有很多精彩的台词。

37
00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:52.870
I won't rapid-fire them right now, but they're some good quotes.
我现在就不连珠炮似地说了，但确实有很多好台词。

38
00:01:53.490 --> 00:02:00.390
Angela, last week when we did grief counseling, we had a lot of bird injuries and fiascos in our life.
安吉拉，上周我们聊《悲伤辅导》时，我们的生活中发生了好多关于鸟类的意外和闹剧。

39
00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:04.310
Has any type of initiation incident happened to you this week?
这周你有没有遇到什么入职仪式之类的事件？

40
00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:07.570
Have I been initiated in my own house?
我在自己家里被“入职”了吗？

41
00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:08.150
Yeah.
对。

42
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:11.750
I mean, talk about an interesting topic if the answer is yes.
我是说，如果答案是肯定的，那这话题可真有意思。

43
00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.430
No, but don't give my kids any ideas.
没有，但别给我孩子们出主意。

44
00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:15.730
They would be all over this.
她们肯定会热衷于此的。

45
00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.310
They'd be like, here's the thing.
她们会说，听着。

46
00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:19.230
Kid club initiation.
儿童俱乐部入职仪式。

47
00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.510
Go into Isabel's room.
去伊莎贝尔的房间。

48
00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:23.390
Put on this fuzzy hat.
戴上这顶毛茸茸的帽子。

49
00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:26.250
Jump backwards three times.
向后跳三次。

50
00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:27.790
Make a duck sound.
学鸭子叫。

51
00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:28.850
You're in the club!
你加入俱乐部了！

52
00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:30.510
Sounds fun.
听起来很有趣。

53
00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:31.390
I'm into it.
我很有兴趣。

54
00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:33.410
All right, let's talk about this episode.
好了，我们来聊聊这一集。

55
00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:34.730
I've got a summary for you.
我为你准备了剧情梗概。

56
00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:35.610
I'm very excited.
我非常兴奋。

57
00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:37.870
This is a big episode, all right?
这一集很重要，明白吗？

58
00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.450
Here's the main storyline.
这是主要剧情线。

59
00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:43.870
Dwight is taking Ryan on his first sales call.
德怀特要带瑞安进行他的第一次销售拜访。

60
00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:46.330
But it's not as simple as that.
但事情没那么简单。

61
00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.270
Of course it's not.
当然没那么简单。

62
00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:48.450
It involves Dwight.
因为涉及到了德怀特。

63
00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.270
It involves a trip to Dwight's farm.
还涉及到了去德怀特的农场。

64
00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:52.130
Yeah.
没错。

65
00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.430
And other places.
还有其他地方。

66
00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.250
And his creepy cousin.
以及他那个令人毛骨悚然的表亲。

67
00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:57.810
Oh, we're going to meet Moe's.
噢，我们要见到莫斯了。

68
00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:02.310
And then, of course, back at Dunder Mifflin, lady, it's pretzel day.
然后，当然了，回到邓德·米夫林公司，女士们，今天是椒盐卷饼日。

69
00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:03.790
That's a big day.
那可是个大日子。

70
00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:05.410
Big day.
大日子。

71
00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.130
Stan Lee is so excited.
斯坦利太兴奋了。

72
00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:08.490
It's a long line.
队伍排得很长。

73
00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:10.330
But they're going to get some pretzels.
但他们还是会去买些椒盐卷饼。

74
00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:16.850
However, at this same time, Jan has told Pam she has to keep a log of Michael's day
然而与此同时，简告诉帕姆，她必须记录下迈克尔一天的行程，

75
00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.790
and make sure he's productive.
并确保他工作效率高。

76
00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:23.050
Meanwhile, over in Stanford, they've got a squeaky chair.
与此同时，在斯坦福分公司，他们有一把吱吱作响的椅子。

77
00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.710
They've got some more flirty flirt.
他们还有更多的调情戏码。

78
00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:25.570
Oh, boy.
天哪。

79
00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:26.590
Let's get into it.
我们开始吧。

80
00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:28.310
Fast fact number one.
速览事实第一条。

81
00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:31.170
As I said, we are going to visit Shroot Farm.
正如我所说，我们要去参观施鲁特农场。

82
00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:32.930
This is huge.
这可是件大事。

83
00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:37.490
We got a ton of questions about this.
我们收到了大量关于这个的问题。

84
00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.150
Are you ready for some names?
准备好听听名字了吗？

85
00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:40.830
I'm ready for some names.
我已经准备好听名字了。

86
00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:41.590
Who wrote in?
是谁发来的？

87
00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:48.730
Lauren Bales, Mike Motherwell, Jessica Cohen, Bailey Lawrence, and Brianna Bullard all said,
劳伦·贝尔斯、迈克·马瑟韦尔、杰西卡·科恩、贝利·劳伦斯和布里安娜·布拉德都问了，

88
00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:50.250
where is the farm?
农场在哪里？

89
00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:53.290
Where is the farm where Ryan and Dwight go?
瑞安和德怀特去的那个农场在哪里？

90
00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:56.070
Well, I know that it was a few places.
嗯，我知道它取景于几个地方。

91
00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.730
Did you hit up some Kentopedia?
你查过肯特百科了吗？

92
00:03:58.330 --> 00:03:59.010
I did.
我查了。

93
00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:06.050
So the main Shroot Farm was shot at the Disney Ranch, which is also called the Golden Oak Ranch.
主要的施鲁特农场是在迪士尼牧场拍摄的，也就是所谓的金橡树牧场。

94
00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:08.750
It is a place where you shoot things.
那是一个专门用来拍摄的地方。

95
00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:14.270
It's like an outdoor exterior shooting studio, basically.
基本上就是一个户外的外景拍摄基地。

96
00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:15.830
It's massive, though.
不过它非常大。

97
00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:16.550
It's massive.
非常大。

98
00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:17.990
It's acres and acres, right?
占地好几英亩，对吧？

99
00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:18.590
It's like...
就像是……

100
00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:18.930
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

101
00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:19.570
It's massive.
它规模宏大。

102
00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:24.950
And so, so many movies that need this sort of rustic look have been filmed there.
而且，有太多需要这种乡村风貌的电影都在那里取景拍摄过。

103
00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:27.410
Like, the history of Disney Ranch is really cool.
比如，迪士尼牧场的历史真的很酷。

104
00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:28.470
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

105
00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:34.290
It's located in Newhall, California, which is about 17 miles from the Dunder Mifflin Studios.
它位于加利福尼亚州的纽霍尔，距离邓德·米夫林工作室大约17英里。

106
00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:39.510
I'm giving you that detail because several people asked how far away it was from our main studios,
我之所以提供这个细节，是因为有几个人问过它离我们的主工作室有多远，

107
00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.490
and I want them to feel satisfied.
我想让他们感到满意。

108
00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:46.150
So there are several barns and farmhouses on this property.
这片土地上有好几座谷仓和农舍。

109
00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:54.210
They chose one of them to be the Shroot Farmhouse, and then they created a graveyard next to it.
他们选中了其中一座作为施鲁特农舍，然后在旁边建了一块墓地。

110
00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:59.010
But you might be thinking, wait a second, I don't remember a graveyard.
但你可能会想，等等，我不记得有墓地啊。

111
00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:01.710
That's because it's a deleted scene.
那是因为那是一段删减片段。

112
00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:03.290
It's a deleted scene.
那是一段删减片段。

113
00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:05.310
It's a really good deleted scene, you guys.
伙计们，那真的是一段很棒的删减片段。

114
00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:07.170
If you have the DVDs, go watch it.
如果你有DVD，一定要去看看。

115
00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:09.030
So here's what happens.
事情是这样的。

116
00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:16.430
They're in the cemetery because Dwight wants to show Ryan how many shroots have actually been buried on shroot farMs.
他们之所以在墓地，是因为德怀特想向瑞安展示到底有多少施鲁特家族的人被埋在施鲁特农场里。

117
00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:22.650
And he has, like, his grandfather's tombstone, and he's like, my grandfather was a good man but did very bad things.
他甚至还带了，比如他祖父的墓碑，他说，我祖父是个好人，但做过非常糟糕的事。

118
00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:24.790
So what is up with his grandfather?
那么他祖父到底是怎么回事？

119
00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:30.930
His grandfather was, I don't know, maybe not a great guy.
他祖父，我不知道，可能不是个什么好人。

120
00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:36.650
Then Dwight finds, like, an empty, it looks like a beer can, and he gets furious.
然后德怀特发现了一个看起来像啤酒罐的东西，他变得非常愤怒。

121
00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:39.770
And he starts looking around, and he sees this couple.
他开始四处查看，然后看到了这对男女。

122
00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:41.950
The guy, like, basically has no clothes on.
那个男的，基本上没穿什么衣服。

123
00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:43.510
He's, like, covering himself with his pants.
他用裤子遮着自己的身体。

124
00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:48.190
And a girl who barely is clothed, and they start running through the field, and Dwight's yelling at them.
还有一个几乎没穿衣服的女孩，他们开始穿过田野逃跑，德怀特冲他们大喊大叫。

125
00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:56.690
And this was awesome because it's a total callback to Office Olympics where Dwight mentions that teenagers sometimes use the beet farm for sex.
这太棒了，因为它完全呼应了《办公室奥运会》里的情节，当时德怀特提到青少年有时会利用甜菜农场做那种事。

126
00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:59.490
Oh, I'm so bummed this is not in the episode.
噢，这段没放进正片里真是太让我失望了。

127
00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:00.970
It's a great scene.
这是一场很棒的戏。

128
00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:02.290
It's a really funny scene.
这是一场非常有趣的戏。

129
00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:02.510
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

130
00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:03.990
I love a callback.
我喜欢这种前后呼应。

131
00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:09.290
And this is calling back creepy grandfather and the teenagers on the farm.
这既呼应了诡异的祖父，也呼应了农场里的青少年。

132
00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:10.690
And you know what?
你知道吗？

133
00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:16.750
When I watched it, all I could think about, since I filmed many scenes on shroot farms, was the field they ran through.
当我观看这段戏时，因为我在施鲁特农场拍过很多戏，我满脑子想的都是他们跑过的那片田野。

134
00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:19.170
A, it was probably super hot.
第一，那里可能超级热。

135
00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:21.110
And B, it was snaky.
第二，那里有很多蛇。

136
00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:22.470
We'll get to that later.
我们稍后再谈这个。

137
00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:27.870
But all I could think of was these people with not a lot of clothes on having to run through that snaky field.
但我满脑子想的都是这些人没穿多少衣服，还得跑过那片多蛇的田野。

138
00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:28.610
I was like, oh.
我当时就想，噢。

139
00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:38.370
Yes, let's talk about those snakes, Angela, because Kent told me that the one requirement for shooting on the ranch is that every production has to hire a snake wrangler.
是的，安吉拉，我们来谈谈那些蛇吧，因为肯特告诉我，在牧场拍摄的一个硬性要求是，每个剧组都必须雇佣一名捕蛇人。

140
00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:38.970
Yeah.
没错。

141
00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:42.630
Because the property has a history of rattlesnakes on the property.
因为这片土地一直有响尾蛇出没。

142
00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:44.030
Yeah.
是的。

143
00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:45.370
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

144
00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:50.350
And Kent said the snake guy found a rattlesnake near that graveyard set.
肯特说，那个捕蛇人在墓地布景附近发现了一条响尾蛇。

145
00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.070
A five-foot rattlesnake, by the way.
顺便说一下，是一条五英尺长的响尾蛇。

146
00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:54.590
Oh, I don't doubt it.
噢，我一点也不怀疑。

147
00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:55.150
I don't doubt it.
我一点也不怀疑。

148
00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:56.890
That's as big as you, Angela.
那和你一样高，安吉拉。

149
00:06:57.070 --> 00:06:58.290
It's my height.
那正好是我的身高。

150
00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:01.590
I have two more facts about Disney Ranch.
关于迪士尼牧场，我还有两个事实要说。

151
00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:02.590
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

152
00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:06.910
So the other location that we shot on Disney Ranch was that barn.
我们在迪士尼牧场拍摄的另一个地点就是那个谷仓。

153
00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:07.670
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

154
00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:10.310
That old barn, we also used that.
那个旧谷仓，我们也用了。

155
00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:18.830
And we used another house at the Disney Ranch for that scene at the bar at the end when Dwight and Ryan are at the bar.
在最后德怀特和瑞安在酒吧的那场戏里，我们还用了迪士尼牧场的另一栋房子。

156
00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:26.750
That house that they used for the bar was originally built for Pee Wee Herman's show back in the 1980s.
那栋被用作酒吧的房子最初是20世纪80年代为皮威·赫尔曼的节目建造的。

157
00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:29.110
And they redressed it and turned it into a bar.
他们重新布置了一下，把它变成了一间酒吧。

158
00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:29.890
Isn't that amazing?
这不是很神奇吗？

159
00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:30.970
That's crazy.
太疯狂了。

160
00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:31.730
I know.
我知道。

161
00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:33.070
So there's a little fun fact.
所以这是一个有趣的小知识。

162
00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:33.730
Yeah.
是啊。

163
00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:42.250
And finally, a lot of people wanted to know if we did keep going back to the same location to shoot year after year.
最后，很多人想知道我们是否年复一年地回到同一个地点拍摄。

164
00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:48.810
And yes, we went back to the Disney Ranch multiple times, including in season four, the money episode.
是的，我们多次回到迪士尼牧场，包括第四季的《钱》那一集。

165
00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:52.030
That is when Pam catches Moe's in the outhouse.
那是帕姆在厕所里抓到莫斯的时候。

166
00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:53.110
Yeah.
没错。

167
00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:54.250
And then we were there.
然后我们就一直在那儿。

168
00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:57.390
Dwight and Angela have a scene in that barn years later.
多年后，德怀特和安吉拉在那个谷仓里还有一场戏。

169
00:07:57.590 --> 00:07:59.850
But then ultimately, we'll get to this.
但最终，我们会讲到那里的。

170
00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:04.210
The final Shroop Farm scene of the whole series is in a whole new location.
整部剧最后一个施鲁特农场的场景是在一个全新的地点拍摄的。

171
00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:06.270
That was so beautiful.
那真是太美了。

172
00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:07.170
But we'll get there.
但我们会讲到那里的。

173
00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:07.950
Yeah.
是啊。

174
00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:08.970
That was gorgeous.
那真是太漂亮了。

175
00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:09.750
It looked like we were in Scotland.
看起来就像我们在苏格兰一样。

176
00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:10.610
It was so beautiful.
真的太美了。

177
00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:11.410
Yes.
是的。

178
00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:13.190
But we don't go there till the end.
但我们要到最后才会去那里。

179
00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:14.330
Till the end end.
最后，真的是最后。

180
00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:17.030
Okay, guys, we'll get there in three years.
好了，伙计们，我们三年后会讲到那里的。

181
00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:17.250
We'll get there.
我们会讲到的。

182
00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:23.630
Fast fact number two, the beet fields were not shot at Disney Ranch.
快速事实之二，甜菜田不是在迪士尼牧场拍摄的。

183
00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.090
That was a completely different location.
那是完全不同的地点。

184
00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:30.910
Those scenes were shot at the Underwood Family Farm in Moorpark, California.
那些场景是在加利福尼亚州穆尔帕克的安德伍德家庭农场拍摄的。

185
00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:34.750
It is a real working 200-acre farm.
那是一个占地200英亩的真实农场。

186
00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:40.230
They grow corn, carrots, kale, strawberries, tomatoes, and, of course, beets.
他们种植玉米、胡萝卜、羽衣甘蓝、草莓、西红柿，当然还有甜菜。

187
00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:44.410
So we filmed those in an actual beet field.
所以我们是在真正的甜菜田里拍摄的。

188
00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:46.210
Isn't that crazy?
这不是很疯狂吗？

189
00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:47.190
That is crazy.
那确实很疯狂。

190
00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:51.330
I have been to that farm with Isabel, my daughter, for a school field trip.
我和我女儿伊莎贝尔去过那个农场参加学校的实地考察。

191
00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:55.670
And I went on a hayride through, like, all around.
我还坐了干草车在周围转了一圈。

192
00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:56.070
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

193
00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:58.470
It's like a huge farm.
那是一个巨大的农场。

194
00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:00.390
And it's just, it's not that far away.
而且离这儿也不远。

195
00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:02.790
All right, moving us along to fast fact number three.
好了，让我们进入快速事实之三。

196
00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:06.170
This was the first episode directed by Randall Einhorn.
这是兰德尔·艾因霍恩执导的第一集。

197
00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:12.610
And you guys, so Randall was our cinematographer and our A-camera operator.
你们知道吗，兰德尔曾是我们的摄影指导和A机位摄影师。

198
00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:14.810
You've heard us talk about him a lot.
你们听我们提起过他很多次了。

199
00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:15.710
We loved him.
我们很爱他。

200
00:09:15.810 --> 00:09:16.510
We loved him.
我们很爱他。

201
00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:17.870
He was just so fun.
他真的太有趣了。

202
00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:20.030
And this was a, this was like a big deal.
而且这可是件大事。

203
00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:24.090
Like, the cast was so excited to see Randall direct an episode.
演员们都非常兴奋能看到兰德尔执导一集。

204
00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:27.230
I got on the phone with Randall, Angela.
安吉拉，我和兰德尔通了电话。

205
00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:27.730
You did.
你通了。

206
00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:28.510
I love him.
我超喜欢他。

207
00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:30.650
Yes, and we're going to have him on the show.
是的，我们打算邀请他上节目。

208
00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:36.910
He told me that this was his first directing job ever.
他告诉我这是他第一次担任导演工作。

209
00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:43.750
He told me that before our show, he had only ever worked on documentary style projects.
他说在我们的剧之前，他只做过纪录片风格的项目。

210
00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:47.530
And remember, we said he was a camera operator on Survivor.
还记得吗，我们说过他是《幸存者》的摄影师。

211
00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:48.230
Yeah.
没错。

212
00:09:48.570 --> 00:09:51.650
But he had done all this other documentary work as well.
但他还做过其他所有的纪录片工作。

213
00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:52.590
Yeah.
是的。

214
00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:58.590
He used to film like, I think like riverboat, crazy river rafting stuff in Australia.
他以前拍过那种，我想是内河船，还有澳大利亚疯狂的漂流之类的东西。

215
00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:00.450
Like, he is like a tough guy.
他就像个硬汉一样。

216
00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:04.830
And I think the documentary style, like we said, was perfect for our show.
我觉得纪录片风格，正如我们所说，非常适合我们的剧。

217
00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:06.550
And now he gets to direct.
现在他终于能执导了。

218
00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:07.730
Yeah.
是啊。

219
00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:12.030
He said he couldn't believe he got the job as our cinematographer because he had never worked
他说他简直不敢相信自己能得到我们剧摄影师的工作，因为他以前从未做过

220
00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:14.130
in scripted anything before.
任何剧本类的工作。

221
00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:17.330
And now Greg was telling him to direct.
而现在格雷格让他去执导。

222
00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:18.650
And he was like, what?
他当时心想，什么？

223
00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:21.290
But he said that Greg was really sweet.
但他提到格雷格人真的很好。

224
00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:27.490
Greg said, Randall, all the time you are finding jokes with your camera.
格雷格说，兰德尔，你一直都在用镜头寻找笑点。

225
00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:30.610
And this is a natural extension of that.
而这正是这一点的自然延伸。

226
00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:34.050
And so Randall was like, all right, I'll do it.
所以兰德尔就想，好吧，我干了。

227
00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:39.130
And he said he was so touched because he felt like everyone in the cast and crew was rooting
他说他非常感动，因为他感觉到所有的演职人员都在支持

228
00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:40.110
for him to succeed.
他取得成功。

229
00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:45.870
He said he'll just never forget what that support felt like and what it meant to him.
他说他永远不会忘记那种支持的感觉，以及它对他意味着什么。

230
00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:49.070
He said, especially BJ, who was the writer of the episode.
他说，特别是BJ，也就是这一集的编剧。

231
00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:54.690
He said the hardest part of directing this episode.
他说执导这一集最难的部分。

232
00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:58.750
Because I said to him, I'm like, Randall, this was a huge episode.
因为我跟他说，兰德尔，这一集太重要了。

233
00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:03.090
You have to introduce Pretzel Day, Shroot Farms, and Moe's.
你得引入椒盐卷饼日、施鲁特农场和莫氏酒吧。

234
00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:06.730
And then it all ends with this epic phone call between Jim and Pam.
最后还要以吉姆和帕姆之间那场史诗般的通话结束。

235
00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:09.250
What was the hardest part of all that?
那这一切中最难的部分是什么？

236
00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:12.850
And he said the hardest part was not holding the camera himself.
他说最难的部分就是不能亲自扛摄像机。

237
00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:14.250
Well, yeah.
嗯，确实。

238
00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:16.350
Yeah, that's so true.
没错，太真实了。

239
00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.850
Because that was his background for years, you know?
因为那是他多年来的背景，你知道吧？

240
00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:22.810
But I think it made him such a great director because he had that vision.
但我认为这让他成为了一位出色的导演，因为他有那种视野。

241
00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:24.510
He knew where he wanted the camera.
他知道他想要摄像机放在哪里。

242
00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:26.690
He knew what he wanted the camera to see.
他知道他想要摄像机拍到什么。

243
00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:27.870
I loved that.
我喜欢这一点。

244
00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:32.930
Well, he said he did take the camera a few times during this episode.
嗯，他说在这一集中他确实有几次拿过了摄像机。

245
00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:34.690
And he even pointed them out to me.
他甚至还指给我看了。

246
00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:38.010
So I'll tell you those moments as we go along.
所以随着节目的进行，我会告诉你们那些时刻。

247
00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:39.050
Oh, fun.
哦，有意思。

248
00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:44.790
And he also told me that even today, when he's directing, because that's what he does now.
他还告诉我，即使是现在，当他在执导时，因为他现在专职做导演了。

249
00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:47.210
He's now a director exclusively.
他现在只做导演了。

250
00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:54.570
And he said it was only last year that he finally directed a project and didn't take the camera once.
他说直到去年，他才终于在执导一个项目时一次都没有去拿摄像机。

251
00:11:55.070 --> 00:11:55.510
Wow.
哇。

252
00:11:56.250 --> 00:12:02.230
But he said that's how he feels it that way still, because those were his beginnings.
但他还是说他就是那种感觉，因为那是他的起点。

253
00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:02.990
Yeah.
是啊。

254
00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:07.330
Well, before he directed this episode, he directed the webisodes.
嗯，在他执导这一集之前，他执导过网络短片。

255
00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:08.730
Oh, yes.
哦，没错。

256
00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:11.810
And so, you know, obviously, that's not like a full episode.
所以，你知道，显然那不像完整的一集。

257
00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:13.910
But I remember how giddy he was.
但我记得他当时有多兴奋。

258
00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:18.390
But he was holding the camera and directing because that was just us on the weekend.
他当时拿着摄像机在执导，因为那只是我们周末拍着玩的。

259
00:12:18.390 --> 00:12:20.270
It was just like three of us there.
当时就我们三个人在那儿。

260
00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:22.690
And you guys won an Emmy for those webisodes.
你们还凭那些网络短片赢得了艾美奖。

261
00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:23.610
We did.
我们确实赢了。

262
00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:24.690
We won an Emmy.
我们赢了一座艾美奖。

263
00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:26.830
I have an Emmy for the accountants.
我有一座属于会计们的艾美奖。

264
00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:27.390
I know.
我知道。

265
00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:28.150
It just tickles me.
这真让我乐不可支。

266
00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:29.070
So cool.
太酷了。

267
00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:29.530
All right.
好吧。

268
00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:31.010
Listen, why don't we take a break?
听着，我们休息一下好吗？

269
00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:34.370
And then we're going to come back and start breaking down this episode.
回来之后我们再开始拆解这一集。

270
00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:35.090
Okay.
好的。

271
00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:45.060
Okay.
好的。

