00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:08.580
I don't know.
我不知道。

304
00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:10.100
It's like they tried something new.
感觉她们像是尝试了什么新花样。

305
00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.100
They tried rollers or something.
她们用了卷发筒之类的东西。

306
00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:14.720
I was like, it looks like hot rollers.
我当时就觉得，看起来像是热卷发筒。

307
00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.220
It looks like hot rollers.
看起来确实像热卷发筒。

308
00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:21.900
I was just like, wait, they were just doing blowouts, and now Jan, Jan is zhuzhing it up
我当时就在想，等等，她们之前不是一直做吹风造型吗，现在简，简竟然在折腾头发了

309
00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:23.540
when she comes in to see Michael now.
当她现在进来见迈克尔的时候。

310
00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.480
That's an interesting take on it.
这观点挺有意思的。

311
00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:32.520
Like, he's talking about the sex he's having with Carol, and she's like, I did not hot roller
就像是，他在说他和卡罗尔发生性关系的事，而她心里想的是，我可不是为了听这个才特意用热卷发筒

312
00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:33.520
my hair for this.
卷了头发的。

313
00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:34.560
For this BS.
为了这些废话。

314
00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:35.260
Yeah.
是啊。

315
00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:38.260
I totally noticed her hair.
我完全注意到了她的头发。

316
00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:45.800
Well, then, Jan goes up to Pam's desk and says that she needs to keep an hourly log of Michael's
嗯，然后简走到帕姆的办公桌前，说她需要记录迈克尔每小时的

317
00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:48.820
activity so that corporate can analyze his productivity.
活动情况，好让总公司分析他的工作效率。

318
00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:54.940
You guys, there's a moment in this scene that made me laugh so hard when I was rewatching it,
伙计们，这一幕里有个瞬间，我重看的时候笑得不行，

319
00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:58.520
and also, I remember breaking every time Melora did it.
而且我记得每次梅洛拉演到那儿我都会笑场。

320
00:14:58.840 --> 00:14:59.040
What?
什么？

321
00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.520
She walks up to the desk.
她走到办公桌前。

322
00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:01.480
I'll tell you.
我告诉你。

323
00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:06.680
She walks up to the desk, and she's like, hi, Pam.
她走到桌前，然后说，嗨，帕姆。

324
00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:08.280
And Pam goes, hi.
帕姆回了句，嗨。

325
00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:09.980
And then she goes, I'm great.
然后她接着说，我很好。

326
00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:13.780
And then keeps talking, but Pam didn't say, how are you?
然后继续说下去，但帕姆根本没问她“你好吗”。

327
00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:14.340
Yeah.
没错。

328
00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:19.700
She's so pissed that Michael has just told her about Carol, and she just walks up with that energy.
她因为迈克尔刚跟她说了卡罗尔的事而气坏了，她带着那种情绪走过来。

329
00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.260
I love it so much.
我太喜欢这个细节了。

330
00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:26.680
So you know I got the shooting drafts for this whole season, and it's in there.
你们知道我拿到了这一整季的拍摄剧本，里面确实有这一句。

331
00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:27.980
I'm great is in there.
“我很好”就在剧本里。

332
00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:31.380
I had to look it up to see if Melora improvised that or if it was written,
我特意查了一下，想看看那是梅洛拉即兴发挥的还是剧本写的，

333
00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:33.420
but that was a written joke, and I love it.
结果那是剧本里写的笑话，我太喜欢了。

334
00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:35.100
So good.
太棒了。

335
00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:38.260
We had some mail about this scene.
我们收到了一些关于这一幕的邮件。

336
00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:43.900
Lauren Hallman wrote in to say, at 1 minute 47 seconds, there's a weird circular object
劳伦·霍尔曼来信说，在1分47秒处，右下角有一个奇怪的圆形物体，

337
00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:48.160
in the bottom right next to an ancient stapler that I can't identify.
就在一个老式订书机旁边，我认不出那是什么。

338
00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:53.360
And Elizabeth Molina said, what's the deal with the scale behind Jenna?
还有伊丽莎白·莫利纳问，珍娜身后的那个秤是怎么回事？

339
00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:57.320
It looks like a food scale, which would make more sense in the kitchen or break room.
看起来像个食物秤，放在厨房或休息室里才比较合理吧。

340
00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.740
I think they're talking about the same object.
我觉得她们说的是同一个东西。

341
00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:01.460
I froze on it.
我把画面定格看了看。

342
00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:02.180
Yeah.
没错。

343
00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:03.740
It is a scale.
那确实是个秤。

344
00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:09.340
I think it's a scale that Pam is using to weigh small packages for mailing.
我觉得那是帕姆用来称小包裹邮寄用的秤。

345
00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:13.680
Yeah, I would think it was probably to make sure she has the right postage.
对，我想大概是为了确保邮资准确吧。

346
00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:15.580
That's what it looked like to me.
我看起来也是这样。

347
00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:16.420
Yeah.
是啊。

348
00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:19.740
We don't have a mail room in our office.
我们的办公室没有专门的收发室。

349
00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:21.300
We have a mail cart.
我们只有一个邮递推车。

350
00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:27.300
So I guess Pam has to keep that scale behind her, but it's not always there.
所以我猜帕姆得把那个秤放在她身后，不过它也不是一直都在那儿。

351
00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:31.500
Listen, we don't know what Pam does back there.
听着，我们不知道帕姆在后面做什么。

352
00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:37.280
With her revolving plants and her scale.
带着她那些轮换的植物和秤。

353
00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:39.720
She can't keep a plant alive.
她根本养不活一盆植物。

354
00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:41.480
She has a giant shredder.
她还有个巨大的碎纸机。

355
00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:42.440
Yeah.
没错。

356
00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:43.840
And now she has a scale.
现在她还有个秤。

357
00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:45.320
We don't know.
我们不知道。

358
00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:46.300
We don't know.
我们不知道。

359
00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:56.400
Well, guys, now we are going to find out that Dwight is taking Ryan on this sales call,
好了，伙计们，现在我们要发现德怀特要带瑞安去跑这趟销售了，

360
00:16:56.560 --> 00:16:58.040
his first sales call.
这是他的第一次销售拜访。

361
00:16:58.320 --> 00:16:59.640
Oh, he's so excited.
噢，他太兴奋了。

362
00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:04.580
There are some great deleted scenes on the DVD that are all about this storyline.
DVD里有一些很棒的删减片段，都是关于这个剧情线的。

363
00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:06.780
But Dwight is so excited.
但德怀特真的太兴奋了。

364
00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:11.460
He's hoping that Ryan will become part of the Dwight's army of champions, right?
他希望瑞安能成为德怀特冠军大军的一员，对吧？

365
00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:12.140
Yeah.
没错。

366
00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:13.900
Not be a slacker like Jim.
而不是像吉姆那样偷懒。

367
00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:17.380
This is like, and maybe, maybe become one of his best friends.
这就像是，也许，也许能成为他最好的朋友之一。

368
00:17:17.860 --> 00:17:18.300
Maybe.
也许吧。

369
00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:21.840
So in the DVDs, there's a deleted scene that I absolutely loved.
在DVD里，有一个我特别喜欢的删减片段。

370
00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:23.420
I laughed so hard.
我当时笑得好大声。

371
00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:25.580
And it's just such a simple moment, you guys.
那只是一个非常简单的瞬间，伙计们。

372
00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:32.060
But Michael goes to hug Ryan to wish him well as he goes out for his first sale.
迈克尔去拥抱瑞安，祝他在第一次销售中好运。

373
00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:34.440
You know, like, I'm going to give you a man hug.
你知道，就像是，我要给你一个男人间的拥抱。

374
00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:35.360
It's awkward.
那很尴尬。

375
00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:36.680
It's so awkward.
太尴尬了。

376
00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:42.100
But then it gets even weirder because then Dwight joins in and he wants to hug him too.
但后来变得更奇怪了，因为德怀特也加入了进来，他也想抱他。

377
00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:45.360
And then Michael's, like, shoving Dwight, like, Dwight, get away.
然后迈克尔就在推德怀特，像是说，德怀特，走开。

378
00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:48.980
Like, meanwhile, like, BJ is, like, stuck between them.
与此同时，BJ就像是被夹在他们中间一样。

379
00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:51.340
It is, it's, it just made me laugh so hard.
真的，这真的让我笑得停不下来。

380
00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.320
I love this whole storyline.
我喜欢整条剧情线。

381
00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:55.240
We know you love it too.
我们知道你也喜欢。

382
00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:56.500
We have a surprise.
我们有个惊喜。

383
00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:58.040
We have a surprise.
我们有个惊喜。

384
00:17:58.220 --> 00:17:58.640
Tell them, Jenna.
告诉他们吧，珍娜。

385
00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:03.680
Rain and BJ are going to come on the show today to talk all about it.
雷恩和BJ今天会来节目，和我们聊聊这件事。

386
00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:05.580
So we're going to break down the rest of the episode.
所以我们要先拆解这一集的剩余部分。

387
00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:11.380
And then when they hop on, they will discuss all things Shrute Farms and the initiation.
等他们加入后，他们会讨论关于舒鲁特农场和入职仪式的一切。

388
00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:13.720
Yes, we're going to skip their scenes for now.
是的，我们暂时先跳过他们的戏份。

389
00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.700
But don't worry, we will get to it.
但别担心，我们之后会讲到的。

390
00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:20.120
For now, let's discuss what's going on at Stanford.
现在，让我们讨论一下斯坦福那边发生了什么。

391
00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:21.280
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

392
00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:28.240
At 3 minutes, 21 seconds, Karen notices that Jim took her chair and has replaced it with the squeaky chair.
在3分21秒时，凯伦注意到吉姆拿走了她的椅子，换成了一把吱吱作响的椅子。

393
00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:29.720
I want you to know something.
我想让你们知道一件事。

394
00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:32.640
Squeaky chair was not in the original script.
吱吱作响的椅子并不是原剧本里的。

395
00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:33.420
Huh.
哈。

396
00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:38.260
The original storyline for Stanford was completely different.
斯坦福的原版剧情线完全不同。

397
00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:39.460
This was a late edition.
这是后来加进去的。

398
00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:45.740
And I traded some text with BJ, and he said he doesn't quite remember where the squeaky chair storyline came from.
我和BJ发过短信，他说他不太记得吱吱作响的椅子这个剧情是怎么来的了。

399
00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:51.920
Let me give you a little pitch where it might have come from, and it might not have.
让我给你们提供一个它可能来源的猜测，虽然也不一定对。

400
00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:59.360
But I want you guys to know something happening behind the scenes was over in the accounting department.
但我希望你们知道，幕后发生的事情是在会计部那边。

401
00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:01.040
And I texted Oscar.
我给奥斯卡发了条短信。

402
00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:02.580
I was like, Oscar, do you remember this?
我说，奥斯卡，你还记得这个吗？

403
00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:04.100
And he just wrote back, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.
他回我说，哈哈哈哈哈。

404
00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:04.760
Okay.
好吧。

405
00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:08.540
There was a crap chair over in accounting.
会计部那边有一把烂椅子。

406
00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.200
It was an absolute piece of crap chair.
那绝对是一把烂透了的椅子。

407
00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:12.900
It wouldn't go up and down.
它没法升降。

408
00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:14.760
It just was like set on one setting.
它就固定在一个高度上。

409
00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:16.860
So it was always way too low for my desk.
所以对我办公桌来说总是太低了。

410
00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:19.400
And then it leaned way too far back.
而且它还总是向后倾斜得太厉害。

411
00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:25.020
So you always felt like, like, I mean, you guys, I know I'm Southern, but I always felt like I was going to get bucked out of it.
所以你总会觉得，伙计们，我知道我是南方人，但我总觉得我会被它甩出去。

412
00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:27.020
I'd be like, that's the chair that's going to buck me out.
我会想，就是这把椅子，它要把我甩出去了。

413
00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:31.060
So sometimes I would go, and it would be at my desk.
所以有时候我过去，发现它就在我的办公桌那儿。

414
00:19:31.180 --> 00:19:33.920
And I'd be like, son of a gun, Oscar switched it again.
我就会说，该死，奥斯卡又把它换过来了。

415
00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:36.280
It just traded back and forth between me and Oscar.
它就在我和奥斯卡之间换来换去。

416
00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:40.100
I would move his chair, and I'd put the crap chair at his desk.
我会把他的椅子挪走，把那把烂椅子放到他的桌子旁。

417
00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:44.460
And then out of nowhere after lunch, it would be back at my desk.
然后午饭后不知怎么的，它又回到了我的桌子旁。

418
00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:48.240
And I'd be like, Oscar, you gave me this piece of crap chair again.
我就会说，奥斯卡，你又把这把烂椅子给我了。

419
00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:51.560
We must have done this, I think, for weeks.
我想我们肯定这样折腾了好几周。

420
00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:54.940
And then one day, I moved it over to Creed's desk.
后来有一天，我把它挪到了克里德的桌子旁。

421
00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.760
Oh, no, Angela.
噢，不，安吉拉。

422
00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:58.120
I did.
我真的这么做了。

423
00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:02.760
And I said to Oscar, I was like, I put it, I put that crap chair at Creed's desk.
我对奥斯卡说，我把它，我把那把烂椅子放到克里德的桌子旁了。

424
00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:03.980
And we, like, laughed.
然后我们就像这样大笑起来。

425
00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:08.440
And anyway, it just cracks me up that this was actually something happening.
总之，这件事竟然真的发生过，这让我觉得特别好笑。

426
00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:10.760
I don't know if the writers ever even knew about it.
我不知道编剧们是否知道这件事。

427
00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:12.360
I don't know if we vented about it.
我不知道我们有没有抱怨过它。

428
00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:15.320
But this was an actual thing happening over in accounting.
但这确实是会计部发生过的真实事件。

429
00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:18.520
Oh, my gosh, you had your own chair war.
天哪，你们竟然还有自己的椅子大战。

430
00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:19.700
We did.
确实有。

431
00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:22.360
But I don't know how Brian stayed out of it.
但我不知道布莱恩是怎么置身事外的。

432
00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:24.880
Maybe because he was too far in the corner.
也许是因为他坐在角落里太远了。

433
00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:25.800
Yeah.
是啊。

434
00:20:25.940 --> 00:20:27.580
It just traded between me and Oscar.
它就在我和奥斯卡之间换来换去。

435
00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:34.680
Well, did you notice in this scene in Stanford when Jim wheels his chair over to the copier?
那么，你在斯坦福的那场戏里注意到吉姆把椅子滑到复印机旁了吗？

436
00:20:34.860 --> 00:20:36.040
Did you look in the background?
你有看背景吗？

437
00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:39.660
I noticed a little something back there.
我注意到了后面的一点小细节。

438
00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:41.880
I saw a few people write in.
我看到有几个人写信提到了。

439
00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:43.840
You have to tell them because I think this is so beautiful.
你必须告诉他们，因为我觉得这太美好了。

440
00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:45.420
All right.
好吧。

441
00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:49.140
I also talked to Randall about this, and he said this was totally on purpose.
我也和兰德尔谈过这件事，他说这完全是故意的。

442
00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:57.220
He planted a guy standing at reception in the same way that Jim would always stand at reception and talk to Pam.
他安排了一个人站在前台，姿势和吉姆以前站在前台跟帕姆聊天时一模一样。

443
00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:03.500
He even has his sleeves rolled up the way Jim used to roll up his sleeves.
他甚至把袖子卷起来的方式都和吉姆以前卷袖子的方式一样。

444
00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:04.500
Sleeve gate.
袖子门事件。

445
00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:06.740
Susan, are you listening to this, Susan?
苏珊，你在听吗，苏珊？

446
00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:07.920
Yeah, I know.
是啊，我知道。

447
00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:09.380
Susan who broke down the sleeves.
就是那个分析袖子的苏珊。

448
00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:10.460
Yeah.
没错。

449
00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:17.720
And Randall said that was on purpose to keep that Pam-Jim thing sort of in our orbit.
兰德尔说那是故意的，为了让帕姆和吉姆的那种感觉留在我们的视线里。

